# omnistream - Multi-platform Live Streaming Middleware

## Project Overview
TypeScript/Node.js middleware providing RESTful APIs to stream RTMP to YouTube, Facebook, TikTok, and Instagram simultaneously. Handles OAuth, scheduling, real-time chat, and message highlighting.

## Architecture Principles
- **Modular providers**: Each platform (YouTube, Facebook, TikTok, Instagram) is completely independent
- **Abstract interfaces**: All providers implement `StreamProvider` interface from `src/core/interfaces.ts`
- **Graceful degradation**: Features work on platforms that support them, fail gracefully on others
- **Per-community OAuth**: Each community has separate OAuth tokens per platform

## Key Files
- `src/core/interfaces.ts` - Core type definitions and interfaces
- `src/providers/youtube/` - YouTube implementation
- `src/providers/facebook/` - Facebook implementation
- `src/providers/tiktok/` - TikTok implementation
- `src/providers/instagram/` - Instagram stub (no official API)
- `src/api/` - RESTful API routes

## Code Standards
- Before commiting code - all tests must pass. 
- **TypeScript strict mode**: All code must be fully typed
- **Error handling**: Always use try-catch and return meaningful errors
- **Testing**: Every provider must have unit tests (Jest) and integration tests (Playwright)
- **Async/await**: Use async/await, never callbacks
- **ESM modules**: Use import/export (not require)

## Platform-Specific Notes

### YouTube
- Full API support for all features
- Use YouTube Data API v3 + YouTube Live Streaming API
- OAuth scopes: `youtube.force-ssl`, `youtube.readonly`

### Facebook
- Use Facebook Graph API
- Live video endpoints available
- Chat via Graph API Live Comments
- OAuth scopes: `pages_manage_posts`, `pages_read_engagement`

### TikTok
- Requires LIVE Access API approval (not generally available)
- Implement stub that returns "not supported" for unapproved features
- Document approval process in README

### Instagram
- NO official live streaming API exists
- Implement stub provider that returns "unsupported" for all methods
- Document limitation clearly

## API Design
- RESTful endpoints under `/api/v1/`
- WebSocket endpoint for real-time chat: `/ws/chat/:streamId`

## Testing Requirements
- **Unit tests**: Mock external API calls
- **Integration tests**: Use Playwright with test OAuth credentials
- Minimum 80% code coverage
- All providers must have identical test structure
- Before commiting code - all tests must pass. 


## Environment Variables
Use `.env` for secrets (never commit):
- `YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID`, `YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET`
- `FACEBOOK_APP_ID`, `FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET`
- `TIKTOK_CLIENT_KEY`, `TIKTOK_CLIENT_SECRET`
- `DATABASE_URL` (for storing OAuth tokens)

## Development Workflow
1. Implement interface in provider class
2. Write unit tests
3. Write integration tests
4. Update API routes
5. Update documentation

## Important Constraints
- Never hardcode credentials
- Always validate input parameters
- Log errors but never expose sensitive data
- Use rate limiting for external API calls
- Cache OAuth tokens appropriately

## Documentation
- Every public method needs JSDoc comments
- README must include API endpoint documentation
- Document platform limitations clearly
